+## Tool-result transformer: `post_tool_transform`
+
+This synchronous transformer runs after a tool succeeds and before the result
+enters model context. It receives a JSON envelope on stdin containing `event`,
+`session_id`, `working_dir`, `tool_name`, `tool_call_id`, `tool_input`,
+`tool_input_file`, `tool_result`, `tool_result_file`, `output_bytes`,
+`output_lines`, `tool_success`, and `swarm`. The stdin envelope is capped at
+256 KB.
+
+When `tool_input` or `tool_result` exceeds the file threshold
+(`post_tool_transform_file_threshold`, default 4096 bytes; env
+`JCODE_HOOK_POST_TOOL_TRANSFORM_FILE_THRESHOLD`), the full content is written to
+a temp file under `jcode-tool-payloads/<session_id>/` and the in-envelope field
+is truncated to the threshold. The `tool_input_file` and `tool_result_file`
+fields are the temp file paths, or `null` when the content fits inline.
+`output_bytes` and `output_lines` are precomputed so a plugin can measure
+output without reading the file. The runtime sweeps old payload files using
+`tool_output_ttl_secs` (default 3600 seconds, env `JCODE_TOOL_OUTPUT_TTL_SECS`).
+
+On success, a transformer may print `{"tool_result":"replacement"}` to stdout.
+Empty or invalid output, a missing key, non-zero exit, spawn failure, or timeout
+fails open and preserves the original result. The default timeout is 500 ms and
+can be changed with `post_tool_transform_timeout_ms`.
+
